# SQLite session state (see backend/db.py). Local runtime data, never committed —
# but the directory itself must exist on a fresh clone, hence the tracked
# .gitkeep. Ignoring the *contents* rather than the directory: git does not
# descend into an ignored directory, so `backend/data/` would make the negation
# below unreachable.
backend/data/*
!backend/data/.gitkeep

